Fillets: the curves of the corner of three blends cut by each other (1653)
are marched the way that keeps their p-curves inside both contacts
(mitcad#1532).

The roof slab rounded on all its edges with 1.1: at the far end's left
eave the intersection of the eave's end edge's blend and the slope's top
edge's blend, marched from where their contacts meet on the end face, left
it tangent to both contacts (both blends touch that face there), and its
p-curves crossed the contacts' p-curves near it (by 0.005 in the blend's
parameters): both blends' wires crossed themselves.

- threeCornerByInter (1653): each pair's intersection is computed from
  where their contacts meet to the point of all three, and where its
  p-curves cross either contact's p-curve to the side away from that point
  (sampled), from that point back; the way crossing least is kept.

